From e6e291166a158ea3c2eca1fd8a3aa90341ca3838 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:33:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Render into and sample heap textures; read ten-bit icons

26 and 27 place Liquid Glass shapes, shadows and panel snapshots in heaps
(type 8, opcode 0x15). A heap is host memory the guest never maps, so a
heap texture has no bytes this device can read. Reims refused them as
render targets (142 refusals on a 26.6.2 boot, 61 on 27.2) and could not
sample them.

A heap texture now renders into a persistent engine resident named by
its own reference: a later pass loads from it, and a sampled bind of the
texture binds the resident. With nothing rendered yet a LOAD starts
undefined, as Metal allows. An abandoned chain has nothing to land for
one. Compute still keeps its own heap residents; a compute-written heap
texture is not yet visible to a draw.

Buffer textures in RGB10A2 and BGR10A2 (26s and 27s panel icons) are
narrowed to RGBA8 by the buffer-texture loader alone; everywhere else the
shared converters keep declining them so the ten bits survive.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
